DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
24138::$$$message_0181_0000_0000$$$::   No one could have hated the first year.::
24139::$$$message_0181_0001_0000$$$::For a long time, he lived a blessed life.[sestop time=3000 nowait=true][lr]::
24140::$$$message_0181_0001_0001$$$::He was born to an ordinary and not particularly affluent household.[lr]::
24141::$$$message_0181_0001_0002$$$::Both his parents and siblings were normal, though he wasn't close in age to his siblings. He would wake up early, help his father work in the forest, and bring the day's harvest back to the village.[lr]::
24142::$$$message_0181_0001_0003$$$::His world was peaceful, his days unchanging.::
24143::$$$message_0181_0002_0000$$$::Their work had gone on for decades.[lr]::
24144::$$$message_0181_0002_0001$$$::His father and his father's father were allowed to reside in the mountain pass. They lived unremarkable lives and died unremarkable deaths.[lr]::
24145::$$$message_0181_0002_0002$$$::He felt the restlessness of youth, but he knew it would pass in time.[lr]::
24146::$$$message_0181_0002_0003$$$::They had a roof over their heads, enough food to avoid starvation, and warm relations with the neighbors. It was a commonplace, fortunate life.::
24147::$$$message_0181_0003_0000$$$::So how did it all go wrong?[lr]::
24148::$$$message_0181_0003_0001$$$::Those plain days were the least of the privileges the villagers allowed them. [l][br]It was a poor village, but everyone lived out their days in peace and quiet.[lr]::
24149::$$$message_0181_0003_0002$$$::The other villagers were no different from them.[lr]::
24150::$$$message_0181_0003_0003$$$::They thought of them as friends.::
24151::$$$message_0181_0004_0000$$$::...Even now, he feels bitter about it.[lr]::
24152::$$$message_0181_0004_0001$$$::Nothing was amiss.[wt canskip=0][lr]::
24153::$$$message_0181_0004_0002$$$::Nothing was wrong.[lr]::
24154::$$$message_0181_0004_0003$$$::The choice was undoubtedly the will of humanity, including his own.::
24155::$$$message_0181_0005_0000$$$::...That's why, even now, he's bitter about it.[lr]::
24156::$$$message_0181_0005_0001$$$::At least let it be the will of Heaven. Then he could curse God's cruelty, instead.::
24157::$$$message_0181_0006_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"You devil!"[font italic=false][lr]::
24158::$$$message_0181_0006_0001$$$::It began without warning.[wm canskip=0][lr]::
24159::$$$message_0181_0006_0002$$$::Done as casually as saying "good morning."[wm canskip=0]::
24160::$$$message_0181_0007_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"Take his eyes first!"[font italic=false][lr]::
24161::$$$message_0181_0007_0001$$$::He was on the way from home to the forest, just like any other day.[lr]::
24162::$$$message_0181_0007_0002$$$::The people he passed on the way ignored his greetings.[lr]::
24163::$$$message_0181_0007_0003$$$::The strangeness was throughout the village.[lr]::
24164::$$$message_0181_0007_0004$$$::Villagers he'd never spoken to surrounded him, and then he never returned to the village again.[wm canskip=0][fg textoff=0 opacity=0 left=139 index=3000 top=284 time=100 storage=074_アンリtext03][lr]::
24165::$$$message_0181_0007_0005$$$::[font italic=true]"Hey, make sure you leave his left eye!"[font italic=false][lr]::
24166::$$$message_0181_0007_0006$$$::They coldly continued the ritual.[lr]::
24167::$$$message_0181_0007_0007$$$::Apparently, he was a devil now.[wm canskip=0][lr]::
24168::$$$message_0181_0007_0008$$$::The villagers lamented, loathed, and eventually raged at this utterly obvious fact, and they decided his fate.[wm canskip=0][fg textoff=0 opacity=0 left=68 index=4000 top=284 time=100 storage=074_アンリtext04][lr]::
24169::$$$message_0181_0007_0009$$$::[font italic=true]"What a racket. Maybe we should crush his throat."[font italic=false][lr]::
24170::$$$message_0181_0007_0010$$$::He felt confusion, more than terror.[lr]::
24171::$$$message_0181_0007_0011$$$::Why?[lr]::
24172::$$$message_0181_0007_0012$$$::Why was this happening?[lr]::
24173::$$$message_0181_0007_0013$$$::How did it come to this?[lr]::
24174::$$$message_0181_0007_0014$$$::Why me?[lr]::
24175::$$$message_0181_0007_0015$$$::No matter how much he thought about it, he couldn't find a reason.[lr]::
24176::$$$message_0181_0007_0016$$$::Just...why?[wm canskip=0][fg textoff=0 opacity=0 left=84 index=5000 top=283 time=100 storage=074_アンリtext05][lr]::
24177::$$$message_0181_0007_0017$$$::[font italic=true]"Yeah, as long as he's still breathing."[font italic=false][lr]::
24178::$$$message_0181_0007_0018$$$::How could they [stoplquake storage=074_アンリtext05][movefg textoff=0 opacity=200 left=200 top=480 time=10 accel=0 storage=074_アンリtext05]do this?[wm canskip=0]::
24179::$$$message_0181_0008_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"Cut the tendons in his arms and legs. Only the tendons. His body belongs to everyone, so we need to leave the rest for them."[font italic=false][lr]::
24180::$$$message_0181_0008_0001$$$::Several people carried out his sentence.[lr]::
24181::$$$message_0181_0008_0002$$$::A bunch of people he knew, who now resented him. They left his limbs intact, even though they weren't limbs anymore.[lr]::
24182::$$$message_0181_0008_0003$$$::They punished his body with the appropriate sentence for denying wealth to their daily lives.[lr]::
24183::$$$message_0181_0008_0004$$$::[font italic=true]"Cut out his tongue. Don't let him die."[font italic=false][lr]::
24184::$$$message_0181_0008_0005$$$::Many people he knew cursed at him and covered him in filth.[lr]::
24185::$$$message_0181_0008_0006$$$::They said he deserved it for threatening their livelihoods, and he had to pay for it with his body.[lr]::
24186::$$$message_0181_0008_0007$$$::[font italic=true]"Serves you right, you damned devil!"[font italic=false][lr]::
24187::$$$message_0181_0008_0008$$$::Any firm personality he had ended there.[lr]::
24188::$$$message_0181_0008_0009$$$::His emotions crumbled under the physical pain.[lr]::
24189::$$$message_0181_0008_0010$$$::His intellect succumbed to the sadness of losing his dignity.::
24190::$$$message_0181_0009_0000$$$::It kept going.[lr]::
24191::$$$message_0181_0009_0001$$$::For how long, he couldn't say.[lr]::
24192::$$$message_0181_0009_0002$$$::He couldn't even moan.[lr]::
24193::$$$message_0181_0009_0003$$$::There was a rotting tree branch in his throat.[lr]::
24194::$$$message_0181_0009_0004$$$::They cut his tongue out long ago.[lr]::
24195::$$$message_0181_0009_0005$$$::His vocal cords were inflamed after the first night of screaming.::
24196::$$$message_0181_0010_0000$$$::People he knew and didn't know all came to vilify him.[lr]::
24197::$$$message_0181_0010_0001$$$::They didn't need a reason to carry out their justice.[lr]::
24198::$$$message_0181_0010_0002$$$::They hated the devil trapped on their mountain with a righteous, unabashed fury.[lr]::
24199::$$$message_0181_0010_0003$$$::They wished he didn't exist.[lr]::
24200::$$$message_0181_0010_0004$$$::They laughed, even though they refused to do him the mercy of killing him.::
24201::$$$message_0181_0011_0000$$$::Hatred called more hatred.[lr]::
24202::$$$message_0181_0011_0001$$$::Finally, he gained a hatred to overcome all his terror and doubt.[lr]::
24203::$$$message_0181_0011_0002$$$::But who could he direct it at?::
24204::$$$message_0181_0012_0000$$$::Why?[lr]::
24205::$$$message_0181_0012_0001$$$::Why?[lr]::
24206::$$$message_0181_0012_0002$$$::Why?[lr]::
24207::$$$message_0181_0012_0003$$$::He doesn't remember how many times he thought or asked that question.[lr]::
24208::$$$message_0181_0012_0004$$$::The noise that came from his throat when they gouged out his eye, when they took scissors to his fingers, was, [font italic=true]why me?[font italic=false][lr]::
24209::$$$message_0181_0012_0005$$$::None of the villagers would tell him.[lr]::
24210::$$$message_0181_0012_0006$$$::Please stop.[lr]::
24211::$$$message_0181_0012_0007$$$::Give it back.[lr]::
24212::$$$message_0181_0012_0008$$$::Someone help.[lr]::
24213::$$$message_0181_0012_0009$$$::He never voiced such desperate wishes.[lr]::
24214::$$$message_0181_0012_0010$$$::Once the thing that used to be his father cut off his last remaining and biggest toe off his left foot, he accepted it.[lr]::
24215::$$$message_0181_0012_0011$$$::He only had one wish left.[lr]::
24216::$$$message_0181_0012_0012$$$::[font italic=true]Why him?[font italic=false] His only wish was to know this, but nobody would tell him.::
24217::$$$message_0181_0013_0000$$$::Once he realized the answer, he truly became a devil.[lr]::
24218::$$$message_0181_0013_0001$$$::There was no reason for him to be the devil.[lr]::
24219::$$$message_0181_0013_0002$$$::No particular reason he was chosen as a sacrifice.[lr]::
24220::$$$message_0181_0013_0003$$$::The village elders, who held the power, didn't even know his face.[lr]::
24221::$$$message_0181_0013_0004$$$::It didn't matter who it was.[lr]::
24222::$$$message_0181_0013_0005$$$::This wasn't some grudge against a serial evildoer,[lr]::
24223::$$$message_0181_0013_0006$$$::nor a rejection of someone who did too much good.[lr]::
24224::$$$message_0181_0013_0007$$$::They just randomly picked him, for no reason whatsoever.[lr]::
24225::$$$message_0181_0013_0008$$$::...A bunch of faceless people ended someone else's life for their own wealth and comfort.[lr]::
24226::$$$message_0181_0013_0009$$$::That's all there was to it.[lr]::
24227::$$$message_0181_0013_0010$$$::They crushed a life with decades left ahead of it to satisfy a single night's greed.[wt canskip=0][current withback=false][stophaze time=100]::
24228::$$$message_0181_0014_0000$$$::                           This world is ruled by people who aren't human.[rf]::
24229::$$$message_0181_0015_0000$$$::Once he understood this, he decided to hate.[lr]::
24230::$$$message_0181_0015_0001$$$::Aŋra Mainiiu: All the Evil in the World.[lr]::
24231::$$$message_0181_0015_0002$$$::The icon they enshrined became a true devil.[lr]::
24232::$$$message_0181_0015_0003$$$::An egg that would never hatch.[lr]::
24233::$$$message_0181_0015_0004$$$::As a savior and Anti-Hero revered only in this cramped world...::
24234::$$$message_0181_0016_0000$$$::...he wasn't free to wriggle his limbs in pain. He had none.[lr]::
24235::$$$message_0181_0016_0001$$$::He was totally dismembered.[lr]::
24236::$$$message_0181_0016_0002$$$::Only his beating heart was still alive.[lr]::
24237::$$$message_0181_0016_0003$$$::He had no limbs. No dignity. He didn't even function as a person anymore, though his sense of pain still worked just fine.[lr]::
24238::$$$message_0181_0016_0004$$$::He accepted all hatred.[lr]::
24239::$$$message_0181_0016_0005$$$::He gave birth to even more hatred.[wm canskip=0]::
24240::$$$message_0181_0017_0000$$$::His shattered persona regained a semblance of order.[lr]::
24241::$$$message_0181_0017_0001$$$::He was a stone.[lr]::
24242::$$$message_0181_0017_0002$$$::No movement was he afforded. No escape from his stone prison could he be given.[lr]::
24243::$$$message_0181_0017_0003$$$::His remaining left eye was pinned open. He could not avert his gaze.[lr]::
24244::$$$message_0181_0017_0004$$$::His dry, cracked eyeball peered out over the world.[lr]::
24245::$$$message_0181_0017_0005$$$::Like a man made of stone. Like a living statue.[wt canskip=0][lr]::
24246::$$$message_0181_0017_0006$$$::Unmoving, he stared at the same scene for months, years, decades.::
24247::$$$message_0181_0018_0000$$$::He couldn't even look away.[lr]::
24248::$$$message_0181_0018_0001$$$::Before his mind went mad with boredom, this would continue until he died forgetting that he was even alive.[wt canskip=0][lr]::
24249::$$$message_0181_0018_0002$$$::The frightening thing was that this torture would be difficult to tolerate for a day, but he would be subject to it for the rest of his life.[lr]::
24250::$$$message_0181_0018_0003$$$::A normal mind would break in seven days.[lr]::
24251::$$$message_0181_0018_0004$$$::How broken his rationality must have been to withstand this and keep his soul intact.[wt canskip=0]::
24252::$$$message_0181_0019_0000$$$::This unchanging scene wouldn't break.[lr]::
24253::$$$message_0181_0019_0001$$$::His village spread out before him.[lr]::
24254::$$$message_0181_0019_0002$$$::He could see the root of all evil, the village of the people who called him a devil and turned him into an actual devil.[lr]::
24255::$$$message_0181_0019_0003$$$::This horde of repulsive goodwill that prospered at the expense of the weak.[lr]::
24256::$$$message_0181_0019_0004$$$::He would hate them as long as he lived.[lr]::
24257::$$$message_0181_0019_0005$$$::The unfairness.[lr]::
24258::$$$message_0181_0019_0006$$$::That ugliness that people refuse to confront.[lr]::
24259::$$$message_0181_0019_0007$$$::He would approve of it, of this great, generous world.[wt canskip=0][current withback=false]::
24260::$$$message_0181_0020_0000$$$::The only thing in his cave was charred hatred.[lr]::
24261::$$$message_0181_0020_0001$$$::There was no trace of a body or personality you could say was him.[lr]::
24262::$$$message_0181_0020_0002$$$::The soul inhabiting his body had long since vanished.[lr]::
24263::$$$message_0181_0020_0003$$$::This was something else.[lr]::
24264::$$$message_0181_0020_0004$$$::Only the hatred born within him smoldered in that flesh now.::
24265::$$$message_0181_0021_0000$$$::How many years went by after that?[lr]::
24266::$$$message_0181_0021_0001$$$::He'd lost his sense of time, so the stagnant world seemed to change at a dizzying pace.[lr]::
24267::$$$message_0181_0021_0002$$$::His point of contact to his old humanity was no exception[line len=2][lr]::
24268::$$$message_0181_0021_0003$$$::The people who choose him, the people who cut off his limbs, the people who were his parents, the people who hated him, and the people he loved...[lr]::
24269::$$$message_0181_0021_0004$$$::Even he couldn't keep hating those people forever.[lr]::
24270::$$$message_0181_0021_0005$$$::The people who took everything from him left the world before he did.::
24271::$$$message_0181_0022_0000$$$::...Like shooting stars.[lr]::
24272::$$$message_0181_0022_0001$$$::The ferociousness of a momentary ruthlessness and the unchanging days were burned into his eye.[lr]::
24273::$$$message_0181_0022_0002$$$::A long time passed.[lr]::
24274::$$$message_0181_0022_0003$$$::He was left alone.::
24275::$$$message_0181_0023_0000$$$::He saw many lives.[lr]::
24276::$$$message_0181_0023_0001$$$::Too many lives, all with too little meaning.[lr]::
24277::$$$message_0181_0023_0002$$$::They consumed time and space, lived fast and recklessly, had children, built wealth, and ended without leaving anything behind.[lr]::
24278::$$$message_0181_0023_0003$$$::They were hollow, but not quite nothing.[lr]::
24279::$$$message_0181_0023_0004$$$::Lives end, but someone can still pick up where they leave off.::
24280::$$$message_0181_0024_0000$$$::Days pass.[lr]::
24281::$$$message_0181_0024_0001$$$::Lives wither and blossom.[lr]::
24282::$$$message_0181_0024_0002$$$::Prosperity and decline repeat.[lr]::
24283::$$$message_0181_0024_0003$$$::He watched as the scenes changed at a frantic pace.[lr]::
24284::$$$message_0181_0024_0004$$$::Believers conquered people of different faiths.[lr]::
24285::$$$message_0181_0024_0005$$$::Communities took in new blood and flourished.[lr]::
24286::$$$message_0181_0024_0006$$$::He watched it all with hatred.[lr]::
24287::$$$message_0181_0024_0007$$$::The only way he could have some type of relationship with them was by hating them.::
24288::$$$message_0181_0025_0000$$$::   [font italic=true]Evil resides in the mountain summit, bedeviling us.[font italic=false][lr]::
24289::$$$message_0181_0025_0001$$$::It became a tradition passed down in his ancient village.[lr]::
24290::$$$message_0181_0025_0002$$$::As long as he hated and as long as he was hated, he would never die.[lr]::
24291::$$$message_0181_0025_0003$$$::The new villagers hated, worshipped, and thanked him as an enemy.[lr]::
24292::$$$message_0181_0025_0004$$$::The young man who became a devil didn't even exist anymore.::
24293::$$$message_0181_0026_0000$$$::Just unproductive hatred.[lr]::
24294::$$$message_0181_0026_0001$$$::A blank space to allow their lives to go on smoothly.[lr]::
24295::$$$message_0181_0026_0002$$$::A gap in their lives, a dumping ground for their overflowing emotions.[lr]::
24296::$$$message_0181_0026_0003$$$::What a convenient, meaningless void of insincerity.::
24297::$$$message_0181_0027_0000$$$::The village disappeared in no time at all.[lr]::
24298::$$$message_0181_0027_0001$$$::It neither flourished nor declined.[lr]::
24299::$$$message_0181_0027_0002$$$::As the times changed, so did the people. The mountain village lost its relevance and became a barren ruin.[lr]::
24300::$$$message_0181_0027_0003$$$::Everything he hated was gone.[lr]::
24301::$$$message_0181_0027_0004$$$::He lost his name and body. He even lost sight of his soul.[lr]::
24302::$$$message_0181_0027_0005$$$::In the end, even hatred had left him behind.::
24303::$$$message_0181_0028_0000$$$::But he was still connected to this place.[lr]::
24304::$$$message_0181_0028_0001$$$::Many months and years passed.[lr]::
24305::$$$message_0181_0028_0002$$$::The people and village were gone. His body was dead. But he still couldn't move from this place.[lr]::
24306::$$$message_0181_0028_0003$$$::The hatred burned into him was unchanging and eternal.[lr]::
24307::$$$message_0181_0028_0004$$$::It would continue as long as the human world continued.[lr]::
24308::$$$message_0181_0028_0005$$$::He would watch from this empty wasteland forever...[lr]::
24309::$$$message_0181_0028_0006$$$::   Until the world ended.::
24310::$$$message_0181_0029_0000$$$::                                      ...and then, I finally open my eyes.::
24311::$$$message_0181_0030_0000$$$::"Hah, ahhh...!!!"[lr]::
24312::$$$message_0181_0030_0001$$$::"Weh!?"[lr]::
24313::$$$message_0181_0030_0002$$$::I jump out of the sofa.[lr]::
24314::$$$message_0181_0030_0003$$$::I have a splitting headache. I'm still disoriented. [noise opacity=158]This room should be familiar, but it looks like a battlefield in the middle of an airstrike.[lr]::
24315::$$$message_0181_0030_0004$$$::"Ah, ahhh...!!!"[lr]::
24316::$$$message_0181_0030_0005$$$::I stand up and swing my right arm, running.[lr]::
24317::$$$message_0181_0030_0006$$$::I swing my right arm wildly, like a person on fire, trying to drive off my delusions, [se storage=se044.wav]heading for the corner of the room.::
24318::$$$message_0181_0031_0000$$$::"Woah, what's going on? Did a spider land on your back?"[lr]::
24319::$$$message_0181_0031_0001$$$::A Servant is sitting in the corner, [se storage=se422.wav]like he always does.[lr]::
24320::$$$message_0181_0031_0002$$$::I don't have the time or affection to answer him.[lr]::
24321::$$$message_0181_0031_0003$$$::I push him aside[line len=2]not even sure why, myself[line len=2]and stand in front of my image.::
24322::$$$message_0181_0032_0000$$$::"Hah, hah...ah..."[lr]::
24323::$$$message_0181_0032_0001$$$::The image in the mirror is the same as the first time I looked into it.[lr]::
24324::$$$message_0181_0032_0002$$$::Nothing's wrong.[lr]::
24325::$$$message_0181_0032_0003$$$::There isn't anything strange about me.[lr]::
24326::$$$message_0181_0032_0004$$$::But, I'm sure that...[lr]::
24327::$$$message_0181_0032_0005$$$::The first time I looked into this mirror, something was wrong...::
24328::$$$message_0181_0033_0000$$$::                                        "What's wrong with your arm?"::
24329::$$$message_0181_0034_0000$$$::"Arm... My left hand..."[lr]::
24330::$$$message_0181_0034_0001$$$::I'm dizzy.[lr]::
24331::$$$message_0181_0034_0002$$$::Something trapped inside me spills out.[lr]::
24332::$$$message_0181_0034_0003$$$::I did notice it back then.[lr]::
24333::$$$message_0181_0034_0004$$$::There was something extra on me in the mirror, and something that should have been there was missing.[lr]::
24334::$$$message_0181_0034_0005$$$::Isn't the reason that wrongness feels vague...::
24335::$$$message_0181_0035_0000$$$::"Feeling better? Then let's keep going.[lr]::
24336::$$$message_0181_0035_0001$$$::You and I both don't like getting our asses kicked, right?"[lr]::
24337::$$$message_0181_0035_0002$$$::...because of the Servant laughing behind me?::
24338::$$$message_0181_0036_0000$$$::I avoid his eyes and look into the mirror.[lr]::
24339::$$$message_0181_0036_0001$$$::My mind's still in shambles, and I can't concentrate enough to stop the dizziness.[lr]::
24340::$$$message_0181_0036_0002$$$::In my tense, flickering vision,[lr]::
24341::$$$message_0181_0036_0003$$$::I see an unpleasant hallucination.::
24342::$$$message_0181_0037_0000$$$::"Hah...hah...hah... Ah."[lr]::
24343::$$$message_0181_0037_0001$$$::My breathing finally becomes more regular.[lr]::
24344::$$$message_0181_0037_0002$$$::I touch my left arm with my right hand.[lr]::
24345::$$$message_0181_0037_0003$$$::It was just a hallucination. I still have my left arm.[lr]::
24346::$$$message_0181_0037_0004$$$::But I still can't shake the feeling of wrongness.::
24347::$$$message_0181_0038_0000$$$::"Huh? What's up with your arm?"[lr]::
24348::$$$message_0181_0038_0001$$$::His voice comes from behind.[lr]::
24349::$$$message_0181_0038_0002$$$::My mind begins to speed up again, just after I'd calmed it down.[lr]::
24350::$$$message_0181_0038_0003$$$::"Nothing. More importantly, you."[lr]::
24351::$$$message_0181_0038_0004$$$::I turn around.[lr]::
24352::$$$message_0181_0038_0005$$$::I open my eyes and fix him with a stare.[lr]::
24353::$$$message_0181_0038_0006$$$::The boy is smiling like a clown.[lr]::
24354::$$$message_0181_0038_0007$$$::His face might be more familiar to someone else.::
24355::$$$message_0181_0039_0000$$$::"I see. So you met another Master during the day."[lr]::
24356::$$$message_0181_0039_0001$$$::...He knows.[lr]::
24357::$$$message_0181_0039_0002$$$::This Servant's known everything all along.[lr]::
24358::$$$message_0181_0039_0003$$$::I realized that already, but I still...[lr]::
24359::$$$message_0181_0039_0004$$$::"That's why I warned you about going out during the day. Oh, well. That girl was telling the truth. The Holy Grail War they sent you here for ended half a year ago."[lr]::
24360::$$$message_0181_0039_0005$$$::I trusted this Servant...!::
24361::$$$message_0181_0040_0000$$$::"Then the Holy Grail War happening now is..."[lr]::
24362::$$$message_0181_0040_0001$$$::"There's someone else besides us.[lr]::
24363::$$$message_0181_0040_0002$$$::No, you're smart enough to have figured that out right away. But you lied to yourself, even sealing your own memories, and tried to keep playing house."::
24364::$$$message_0181_0041_0000$$$::"This is a weight off my back, though.[lr]::
24365::$$$message_0181_0041_0001$$$::Can we drop it already, Master?[lr]::
24366::$$$message_0181_0041_0002$$$::For this whole farce, you've been dragging out everyone who's already retired just so you can keep having your Holy Grail War!"[lr]::
24367::$$$message_0181_0041_0003$$$::He cackles.[lr]::
24368::$$$message_0181_0041_0004$$$::...It's grating.[lr]::
24369::$$$message_0181_0041_0005$$$::It grates, [clfg][fg index=2000 pos=c storage=士郎アンリ02d(中)][fg left=0 index=1000 top=0 storage=iバゼットの隠れ家_内部-(深夜)][dash textoff=0 page=back mx=0 opacity=255 layer=all irot=-0.0 cx=310 imag=3.9 time=100 cy=571 mag=3.9 my=0 rot=-0.0 accel=0][noise_back][transex textoff=0 time=200]it grates, [clfg][fg index=2000 pos=c storage=士郎アンリ02d(中)][fg left=0 index=1000 top=0 storage=iバゼットの隠れ家_内部-(深夜)][dash textoff=0 page=back mx=0 opacity=255 layer=all irot=-0.0 cx=364 imag=1.9 time=100 cy=66 mag=1.9 my=0 rot=-0.0 accel=0][noise_back][transex textoff=0 time=200]it grates...!::
24370::$$$message_0181_0042_0000$$$::"You...you tricked me, [wvl][se storage=se230.wav][shock vmax=25 time=400 count=-3]Avenger!!!"[lr]::
24371::$$$message_0181_0042_0001$$$::"Now that's not very nice. You never asked. If you'd asked me how the Fifth Holy Grail War ended, I would've told you about how you [block len=4]."::
24372::$$$message_0181_0043_0000$$$::   It hurts.[lr]::
24373::$$$message_0181_0043_0001$$$::My confused head is in pain. [wait canskip=false time=600]As my eyes look at him, they are in pain. [wait canskip=false time=600]My unstable breathing is a reason why my heart is in pain.[lr]::
24374::$$$message_0181_0043_0002$$$::And worst of all, [wait canskip=false time=600]my left arm throbs, [wait canskip=false time=800]like someone just cut it off.::
24375::$$$message_0181_0044_0000$$$::"You have a painful look on    [stopnoise]but you should feel better after a little    [noise opacity=128]. It was a rocky  [stopnoise]but now that you've figured it      [noise opacity=60]you can..."[lr]::
24376::$$$message_0181_0044_0001$$$::The shadow reaches out with its hand.[lr]::
24377::$$$message_0181_0044_0002$$$::A sensation in my left arm feels like knives in my brain.[lr]::
24378::$$$message_0181_0044_0003$$$::"...Shut up. How dare you..."[lr]::
24379::$$$message_0181_0044_0004$$$::I thought I could trust you. That you were a brother-in-arms.[lr]::
24380::$$$message_0181_0044_0005$$$::"You betrayed me too...!"::
24381::$$$message_0181_0045_0000$$$::The instant I say the words, I can't think straight anymore.[lr]::
24382::$$$message_0181_0045_0001$$$::My legs start running without a destination in mind, like I can't stand being there or even existing anymore.[lr]::
24383::$$$message_0181_0045_0002$$$::Like I'm running from something.[lr]::
24384::$$$message_0181_0045_0003$$$::Shattered, disorganized memories and the pain of an invisible bleeding wound on my left arm prevent my mind from working.::
24385::$$$message_0181_0046_0000$$$::   I can't remember.[lr]::
24386::$$$message_0181_0046_0001$$$::I'm sure I heard her, but I can't remember my conversation with that girl.[lr]::
24387::$$$message_0181_0046_0002$$$::She said someone died.[lr]::
24388::$$$message_0181_0046_0003$$$::Someone died, and the Fifth Holy Grail War was over.[lr]::
24389::$$$message_0181_0046_0004$$$::Died?[lr]::
24390::$$$message_0181_0046_0005$$$::Who?::
24391::$$$message_0181_0047_0000$$$::I ran that time, too.[lr]::
24392::$$$message_0181_0047_0001$$$::I didn't move when she said the war was over,[lr]::
24393::$$$message_0181_0047_0002$$$::so why did something so trivial shake me so badly?::
24394::$$$message_0181_0048_0000$$$::"Hah... Hah, hah, hah...!"[lr]::
24395::$$$message_0181_0048_0001$$$::I run.[lr]::
24396::$$$message_0181_0048_0002$$$::I don't know where I'm going, but I'm running toward a definite destination.[lr]::
24397::$$$message_0181_0048_0003$$$::My left arm feels like it's about to tear off.[lr]::
24398::$$$message_0181_0048_0004$$$::The pain invades my thoughts, and I can't shake off the confusion.[wm canskip=0]::
24399::$$$message_0181_0049_0000$$$::When I left my hometown,[lr]::
24400::$$$message_0181_0049_0001$$$::I was a curio with no place in the Association.[lr]::
24401::$$$message_0181_0049_0002$$$::The more I showed my worth, the more they shunned me.[lr]::
24402::$$$message_0181_0049_0003$$$::After I went far away and realized how much I loved my hometown, there was no way home.[lr]::
24403::$$$message_0181_0049_0004$$$::I had nothing certain in my life. Even my sense of self was vague. I made my appearance alone impressive, and that day, I found a strength I could count on.[lr]::
24404::$$$message_0181_0049_0005$$$::I decided that I didn't need anyone else.[lr]::
24405::$$$message_0181_0049_0006$$$::Things would be so much easier if that were true, I pined selfishly.::
24406::$$$message_0181_0050_0000$$$::"Hah, guh...! Aah, [wvl][shock vmax=20 time=600 count=-4]ah, ha, ah...!"[lr]::
24407::$$$message_0181_0050_0001$$$::The pain twists my mind.[lr]::
24408::$$$message_0181_0050_0002$$$::I have morphine in my bag. This is the first time I've wanted to not feel the pain. But I can't inject this into my left arm. I wish I could get an epidural so it could hit my brain immediately and I'd forget everything.::
24409::$$$message_0181_0051_0000$$$::Forget. Forget. Forget it all.[lr]::
24410::$$$message_0181_0051_0001$$$::I don't want to hear who died.[lr]::
24411::$$$message_0181_0051_0002$$$::I came to this town as a Master. That man doesn't matter to me.::
24412::$$$message_0181_0052_0000$$$::    Ahh, but why did I become a Master?[lr]::
24413::$$$message_0181_0052_0001$$$::Bazett Fraga McRemitz is a Seal Designation Enforcer. Getting sent to this Far Eastern country for a Holy Grail War seems out of my area of expertise, no matter how you slice it.[lr]::
24414::$$$message_0181_0052_0002$$$::There was a reason.[lr]::
24415::$$$message_0181_0052_0003$$$::There had to be a reason for it.[lr]::
24416::$$$message_0181_0052_0004$$$::That reason made me happy, happy to reunite after years, and I, I...::
24417::$$$message_0181_0053_0000$$$::                                         What a mess. (Who died?)[nolr][wait canskip=0 time=600]::
24418::$$$message_0181_0053_0001$$$::                    What a mess. (Who died?)[nolr][wait canskip=0 time=600]::
24419::$$$message_0181_0053_0002$$$::                                                             What a mess...! (Who died...!?)[nolr][wait canskip=0 time=1200]::
24420::$$$message_0181_0053_0003$$$::I've arrived.[lr]::
24421::$$$message_0181_0053_0004$$$::This is a place I never entered before.[lr]::
24422::$$$message_0181_0053_0005$$$::A place I always wanted to go.[lr]::
24423::$$$message_0181_0053_0006$$$::From what I've heard, it's a small but stately chapel.[lr]::
24424::$$$message_0181_0053_0007$$$::It's imposing but not ostentatious. Very like them to design it that way.[lr]::
24425::$$$message_0181_0053_0008$$$::The furnishings are practical and it gives off a tense aura. Just like him.[lr]::
24426::$$$message_0181_0053_0009$$$::I see the figure of a man I trusted. The sight is nostalgic to me even now.::
24427::$$$message_0181_0054_0000$$$::Yes, why didn't I come here sooner?[lr]::
24428::$$$message_0181_0054_0001$$$::This is his place.[lr]::
24429::$$$message_0181_0054_0002$$$::During the Fifth Holy Grail War, that priest always welcomed visitors[line len=2]::
24430::$$$message_0181_0055_0000$$$::...Huh?[lr]::
24431::$$$message_0181_0055_0001$$$::This isn't what I heard.[lr]::
24432::$$$message_0181_0055_0002$$$::Instead, I see a girl I don't know waiting for me in a ruined building.::
24433::$$$message_0181_0056_0000$$$::"Who are you...?"[lr]::
24434::$$$message_0181_0056_0001$$$::My pain reaches a fever pitch.[lr]::
24435::$$$message_0181_0056_0002$$$::My left arm feels like it could fall off.[lr]::
24436::$$$message_0181_0056_0003$$$::"I'm standing in for the father. Kirei Kotomine is not here. He's not anywhere in this world, anymore.[lr]::
24437::$$$message_0181_0056_0004$$$::Wake up, Bazett. The thing you wished for never existed. Just as Kirei Kotomine has never loved you."::
24438::$$$message_0181_0057_0000$$$::"...Ah."[lr]::
24439::$$$message_0181_0057_0001$$$::I was chosen because he recommended me.[lr]::
24440::$$$message_0181_0057_0002$$$::"The overseer asked for you directly. Do you happen to have a personal friendship with him, Bazett?"[lr]::
24441::$$$message_0181_0057_0003$$$::It wasn't a mean-spirited move by the Association.[lr]::
24442::$$$message_0181_0057_0004$$$::I was happy he chose me, when he never chooses anyone.::
24443::$$$message_0181_0058_0000$$$::"...Aahh."[lr]::
24444::$$$message_0181_0058_0001$$$::But no one said what would happen afterward.[lr]::
24445::$$$message_0181_0058_0002$$$::As far as mixing business and pleasure went, it was a disappointment.[lr]::
24446::$$$message_0181_0058_0003$$$::He recommended me as a Master for my abilities.[lr]::
24447::$$$message_0181_0058_0004$$$::That's why, I hoped to win the war and see him again.[lr]::
24448::$$$message_0181_0058_0005$$$::Only I planned to meet with him next time as the victor of the Holy Grail War.::
24449::$$$message_0181_0059_0000$$$::"Aaahhh...ah."[lr]::
24450::$$$message_0181_0059_0001$$$::Everything was going so well.[lr]::
24451::$$$message_0181_0059_0002$$$::I made a pact with my ideal Servant and found a mage's former dwelling to use as my hideout.[lr]::
24452::$$$message_0181_0059_0003$$$::The seven Servants would be assembled soon. Just when I was hyping myself up for the war to come, he came to that room, and...[wt canskip=0]::
24453::$$$message_0181_0060_0000$$$::"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH!!!"[lr]::
24454::$$$message_0181_0060_0001$$$::He killed me.[wt canskip=0][current withback=false]::
24455::$$$message_0181_0061_0000$$$::I remember.[lr]::
24456::$$$message_0181_0061_0001$$$::Those were my last moments.[lr]::
24457::$$$message_0181_0061_0002$$$::The end of a pathetic Master who was called to the Holy Grail War and didn't even take part in it.::
24458::$$$message_0181_0062_0000$$$::[font italic=true]"For this whole farce, you've been dragging out everyone who's already retired..."[font italic=false][lr]::
24459::$$$message_0181_0062_0001$$$::Avenger was right.[lr]::
24460::$$$message_0181_0062_0002$$$::Kotomine backstabbed me in that house.[lr]::
24461::$$$message_0181_0062_0003$$$::He plucked the Command Spells from my left arm and left me to rot.::
24462::$$$message_0181_0063_0000$$$::It was a critical wound that would've killed me if I'd moved at all.[lr]::
24463::$$$message_0181_0063_0001$$$::But since I couldn't move, I could only wait for death.[lr]::
24464::$$$message_0181_0063_0002$$$::As I bled out, my fading consciousness made a wish on the verge of death.::
24465::$$$message_0181_0064_0000$$$::Not out of vengeance.[lr]::
24466::$$$message_0181_0064_0001$$$::I didn't have the energy to feel anger at my betrayal, as death caught up to me.[lr]::
24467::$$$message_0181_0064_0002$$$::Not out of despair.[lr]::
24468::$$$message_0181_0064_0003$$$::I didn't feel any sadness at my betrayal, as I began to black out.[lr]::
24469::$$$message_0181_0064_0004$$$::In that moment, the only obstinate feeling I had in my heart was...[lr]::
24470::$$$message_0181_0064_0005$$$::"I don't want to die."::
24471::$$$message_0181_0065_0000$$$::I don't want to die here.[lr]::
24472::$$$message_0181_0065_0001$$$::I don't want to die such a pathetic death.[lr]::
24473::$$$message_0181_0065_0002$$$::I couldn't bear to die alone.[lr]::
24474::$$$message_0181_0065_0003$$$::In that paused moment, mostly dead, I kept screaming for that until my life ran out.::
24475::$$$message_0181_0066_0000$$$::And something answered.[lr]::
24476::$$$message_0181_0066_0001$$$::"...If you'll become my Master..."[rf][lr]::
24477::$$$message_0181_0066_0002$$$::I heard it.[lr]::
24478::$$$message_0181_0066_0003$$$::"...then I'll make your wish a reality, and it will remain that way as long as our pact continues."[rf][lr]::
24479::$$$message_0181_0066_0004$$$::The voice of something unidentified.::
24480::$$$message_0181_0067_0000$$$::It was probably the thing that used to be the Holy Grail.[lr]::
24481::$$$message_0181_0067_0001$$$::The formless void inside the Holy Grail, which was destroyed by the winner of the fifth war.[lr]::
24482::$$$message_0181_0067_0002$$$::Normally, it should have returned to the Throne of Heroes after the Holy Grail collapsed.[lr]::
24483::$$$message_0181_0067_0003$$$::But it was still inside, alive.[lr]::
24484::$$$message_0181_0067_0004$$$::No, inside the Holy Grail which grants people's wishes, it finally became the hero people wished for.[lr]::
24485::$$$message_0181_0067_0005$$$::It was reborn as a Servant inside the Holy Grail.[lr]::
24486::$$$message_0181_0067_0006$$$::A demon, a Holy Grail granting humanity's wishes, called All the Evil in the World, answered my call.::
24487::$$$message_0181_0068_0000$$$::Incarnation of the Holy Grail it might be, but it was still a Servant. It needed a Master or it would disappear.[lr]::
24488::$$$message_0181_0068_0001$$$::After this impossible miracle, this coincidence that would never happen again, it finally became the hero everyone asked for, but it wouldn't even last a single night.[lr]::
24489::$$$message_0181_0068_0002$$$::In that moment, neither of us had a future.[lr]::
24490::$$$message_0181_0068_0003$$$::Of course...[lr]::
24491::$$$message_0181_0068_0004$$$::I'd already passed that threshold.::
24492::$$$message_0181_0069_0000$$$::I was totally lost.[lr]::
24493::$$$message_0181_0069_0001$$$::I didn't even have the capacity to wonder what it was.[lr]::
24494::$$$message_0181_0069_0002$$$::I was just afraid.[lr]::
24495::$$$message_0181_0069_0003$$$::Afraid that after my death, my body would rot and wither away, leaving nothing left of me.[lr]::
24496::$$$message_0181_0069_0004$$$::So I ignited that flawed conviction, on the verge of death.[lr]::
24497::$$$message_0181_0069_0005$$$::I don't want to die.[lr]::
24498::$$$message_0181_0069_0006$$$::I want to continue our pact.::
24499::$$$message_0181_0070_0000$$$::The thing that lost its container, the Holy Grail, made a pact with me as its new container.[lr]::
24500::$$$message_0181_0070_0001$$$::The moment the pact was struck, I fainted.[lr]::
24501::$$$message_0181_0070_0002$$$::I died.::
24502::$$$message_0181_0071_0000$$$::So the thing left here is my corpse.[lr]::
24503::$$$message_0181_0071_0001$$$::I embraced the mistaken, pitiful hope to keep on playing in this walled garden, repeating these four days forever.[lr]::
24504::$$$message_0181_0071_0002$$$::...Even if my last wish had been to come back to life, it probably couldn't have been granted.[lr]::
24505::$$$message_0181_0071_0003$$$::He told me before: [lr]::
24506::$$$message_0181_0071_0004$$$::the dead can't bring the dead back to life.[lr]::
24507::$$$message_0181_0071_0005$$$::Only the living have the privilege of giving shape to the dead.::
24508::$$$message_0181_0072_0000$$$::...All he could really do was trick my soul.[lr]::
24509::$$$message_0181_0072_0001$$$::He would preserve my soul outside of my body and play a dream based on reality for me on repeat, as long as our pact was intact.[lr]::
24510::$$$message_0181_0072_0002$$$::An excellently furnished dream, at that.[lr]::
24511::$$$message_0181_0072_0003$$$::A cradle-like hollow, built in the depths of my slumber.::
24512::$$$message_0181_0073_0000$$$::...That's right.[lr]::
24513::$$$message_0181_0073_0001$$$::Bazett wished for this never-ending Holy Grail War.[lr]::
24514::$$$message_0181_0073_0002$$$::That Servant was a Holy Grail just for me, who would grant my wish.::
24515::$$$message_0181_0074_0000$$$::I finally arrive at the church a few minutes after Bazett.[lr]::
24516::$$$message_0181_0074_0001$$$::I knew she'd run to the church.[lr]::
24517::$$$message_0181_0074_0002$$$::The church is Bazett Fraga McRemitz's last safe haven.[lr]::
24518::$$$message_0181_0074_0003$$$::I come up to the demon's gate that I shouldn't go through.::
24519::$$$message_0181_0075_0000$$$::"...Tch, I hear the organ. I hope this doesn't turn into a hassle."[lr]::
24520::$$$message_0181_0075_0001$$$::Judging by her mood earlier, she's as close to snapping as her face suggested, but as a Servant, I can't let my Master lose herself to her despair.[lr]::
24521::$$$message_0181_0075_0002$$$::I ready myself to lose my head at any moment, and I grope the door.::
24522::$$$message_0181_0076_0000$$$::A woman stands in the ruins, looking powerless.[lr]::
24523::$$$message_0181_0076_0001$$$::Silver flowers are blooming at the altar.::
24524::$$$message_0181_0077_0000$$$::"Hey there. Looks like you've pretty much remembered everything."[lr]::
24525::$$$message_0181_0077_0001$$$::She doesn't answer.[lr]::
24526::$$$message_0181_0077_0002$$$::She's calmed down, but she still looks mad at me.[wm canskip=0][clfg textoff=0 time=100 storage=カレン修道服無帽01a(遠)]::
24527::$$$message_0181_0078_0000$$$::"Ah, still in a bad mood, milady?[lr]::
24528::$$$message_0181_0078_0001$$$::Fine, I'll give you a freebie. I really shouldn't tell you this unless you ask, but in the spirit of honesty, I'll tell you how this world really works."[lr]::
24529::$$$message_0181_0078_0002$$$::"...I don't need you to do that.[lr]::
24530::$$$message_0181_0078_0003$$$::But you do need to answer two questions for me."::
24531::$$$message_0181_0079_0000$$$::I cut the banter.[lr]::
24532::$$$message_0181_0079_0001$$$::There's no emotion at all in her words.[lr]::
24533::$$$message_0181_0079_0002$$$::She's a machine now.[lr]::
24534::$$$message_0181_0079_0003$$$::Then I don't need to try to be human, either.::
24535::$$$message_0181_0080_0000$$$::"Is it true that the Holy Grail War won't end as long as I wish for it?"[lr]::
24536::$$$message_0181_0080_0001$$$::   YES.[lr]::
24537::$$$message_0181_0080_0002$$$::"And as long as the Holy Grail War goes on, I won't die?"[lr]::
24538::$$$message_0181_0080_0003$$$::   YES.::
24539::$$$message_0181_0081_0000$$$::She spits out an affirmation.[se storage=se198.wav][wait canskip=0 time=500][sestop storage=se198.wav time=4000 nowait=true][clfg textoff=0 storage=バゼット05a(中) rule=シャッター左から time=400][lr]::
24540::$$$message_0181_0081_0001$$$::The woman walks past me toward the church exit.[lr]::
24541::$$$message_0181_0081_0002$$$::...I don't believe this.[lr]::
24542::$$$message_0181_0081_0003$$$::I'm actually surprised right now.::
24543::$$$message_0181_0082_0000$$$::"...Wait. Whaddya mean, 'fine'? You're just going to leave after you got here?"[lr]::
24544::$$$message_0181_0082_0001$$$::"We'll just go back to the first day as always. What are you going on about?"[lr]::
24545::$$$message_0181_0082_0002$$$::...Well, damn.[lr]::
24546::$$$message_0181_0082_0003$$$::Our usual positions are reversed.::
24547::$$$message_0181_0083_0000$$$::"I don't get it. You know how this works.[lr]::
24548::$$$message_0181_0083_0001$$$::Then that should be enough for you. This world's about to die. It won't end, but it won't continue, either. You won't gain anything by staying here, you know."::
24549::$$$message_0181_0084_0000$$$::"That goes for the outside world, too.[lr]::
24550::$$$message_0181_0084_0001$$$::It's all crumbling. Me. This world around me. And the world that allowed this very thing to happen.[lr]::
24551::$$$message_0181_0084_0002$$$::They won't recover. It's just a matter of how long I delay this peaceful doom."::
24552::$$$message_0181_0085_0000$$$::She's afraid.[lr]::
24553::$$$message_0181_0085_0001$$$::Afraid of her certain death.::
24554::$$$message_0181_0086_0000$$$::"We're living in a world without hope or a future. If I have to go back to a world like that, I'd rather keep repeating this one.[lr]::
24555::$$$message_0181_0086_0001$$$::...That's right. I wish I'd realized sooner. I shouldn't let that betrayal get me down. I never had anything to begin with. I'd rather keep living these four days than live in a place like that."::
24556::$$$message_0181_0087_0000$$$::She's wrong.[lr]::
24557::$$$message_0181_0087_0001$$$::It's fine to be weak. But it would be a bit of a waste for her to get stuck here.[lr]::
24558::$$$message_0181_0087_0002$$$::What have you been struggling all this time for?::
24559::$$$message_0181_0088_0000$$$::"So you like it here more? A little late for that.[lr]::
24560::$$$message_0181_0088_0001$$$::You've known your entire life that real life isn't easy."[lr]::
24561::$$$message_0181_0088_0002$$$::She's pessimistic because she's weak.[lr]::
24562::$$$message_0181_0088_0003$$$::But the priest said that accepting that weakness and dying is the most human thing of all.::
24563::$$$message_0181_0089_0000$$$::"...This conversation is over. I'm continuing the war.[lr]::
24564::$$$message_0181_0089_0001$$$::You are my Servant. You just need to do what I say."[lr]::
24565::$$$message_0181_0089_0002$$$::Bazett leaves the church.[lr]::
24566::$$$message_0181_0089_0003$$$::That really was unexpected.[lr]::
24567::$$$message_0181_0089_0004$$$::I thought she'd deny this farce once she got her memories back.::
24568::$$$message_0181_0090_0000$$$::"...Looks like she needs another push."[lr]::
24569::$$$message_0181_0090_0001$$$::But I can't think of anything to motivate her.[lr]::
24570::$$$message_0181_0090_0002$$$::...Oh, well.[lr]::
24571::$$$message_0181_0090_0003$$$::If my Master still wants to fight, then I'll just obediently follow her.[lr]::
24572::$$$message_0181_0090_0004$$$::Giving her one last push is a champion of justice's job.::
24573::$$$message_0181_0091_0000$$$::"You're going to continue?"[lr]::
24574::$$$message_0181_0091_0001$$$::Another woman is at the altar.[lr]::
24575::$$$message_0181_0091_0002$$$::Knowing how sensitive she is, I can't approach any closer or she'll die.[lr]::
24576::$$$message_0181_0091_0003$$$::This is the closest I can get.[lr]::
24577::$$$message_0181_0091_0004$$$::We were never intimate enough with each other to talk or touch, anyway.::
24578::$$$message_0181_0092_0000$$$::"What do you expect from me? My contractor says she wants to continue. If a mere familiar like me were to break our contract, that would break all the mage rules."[lr]::
24579::$$$message_0181_0092_0001$$$::"I understand. That is indeed the best decision, given your position."::
24580::$$$message_0181_0093_0000$$$::We both sound unconcerned.[lr]::
24581::$$$message_0181_0093_0001$$$::Neither of us has any interest in the other, so our conversations are concise.[lr]::
24582::$$$message_0181_0093_0002$$$::But, for some reason...[lr]::
24583::$$$message_0181_0093_0003$$$::"...It seems like she enjoys the fact that she met you."[lr]::
24584::$$$message_0181_0093_0004$$$::...she says something needless.::
24585::$$$message_0181_0094_0000$$$::"Ah... Well, I'm glad someone enjoyed it."[lr]::
24586::$$$message_0181_0094_0001$$$::I give her a vague answer.[lr]::
24587::$$$message_0181_0094_0002$$$::Should I be happy? Jealous? Frustrated? Sad?[lr]::
24588::$$$message_0181_0094_0003$$$::To be honest, I don't know what the correct reaction is.::
24589::$$$message_0181_0095_0000$$$::"My Master's waiting outside. I'm leaving."[lr]::
24590::$$$message_0181_0095_0001$$$::This feels like it's going to get awkward, so I beat a hasty retreat.::
24591::$$$message_0181_0096_0000$$$::"...Allow me to warn you.[lr]::
24592::$$$message_0181_0096_0001$$$::Whether you sever your pact or continue until some kind of conclusion can be reached, neither scenario will save her.[lr]::
24593::$$$message_0181_0096_0002$$$::You may as well keep[line len=2]"[lr]::
24594::$$$message_0181_0096_0003$$$::I don't want to hear the rest.[lr]::
24595::$$$message_0181_0096_0004$$$::To begin with, what she's saying is incorrect.::
24596::$$$message_0181_0097_0000$$$::"No way. No one is beyond salvation. But they have to wish for it.[lr]::
24597::$$$message_0181_0097_0001$$$::Everything gets saved in the end, you know."[lr]::
24598::$$$message_0181_0097_0002$$$::"...I'm amazed you would say that, Aŋra Mainiiu."[lr]::
24599::$$$message_0181_0097_0003$$$::"Of course. The salvation I'm talking about isn't for humans, though."::
24600::$$$message_0181_0098_0000$$$::Unfortunately, I don't know any way to save someone while they're alive.[lr]::
24601::$$$message_0181_0098_0001$$$::You can't change something that's fallen to despair.[lr]::
24602::$$$message_0181_0098_0002$$$::But you can at least swap the despair for something more meaningful.[lr]::
24603::$$$message_0181_0098_0003$$$::In someone's dying moments, at the last possible second...[lr]::
24604::$$$message_0181_0098_0004$$$::...if they can get drunk on thinking they lived a good life, then they'll die happy.::
24605::$$$message_0181_0099_0000$$$::"...Hey. Do you still want to put an end to this wish?"[lr]::
24606::$$$message_0181_0099_0001$$$::"Of course I do. How many billions of loops do you think I've done so far? I'm sick and tired of this dead-end street."[lr]::
24607::$$$message_0181_0099_0002$$$::"Liar."[lr]::
24608::$$$message_0181_0099_0003$$$::She goes up the stairs.[lr]::
24609::$$$message_0181_0099_0004$$$::I'm left alone in the chapel.::
24610::$$$message_0181_0100_0000$$$::"...Billions of times, huh?"[lr]::
24611::$$$message_0181_0100_0001$$$::I've seen and learned everything there is about these peaceful days.[lr]::
24612::$$$message_0181_0100_0002$$$::Each time I learn of a new event, it loses its luster.[lr]::
24613::$$$message_0181_0100_0003$$$::It's a world I know everything about, though I'm not experiencing any of it.[lr]::
24614::$$$message_0181_0100_0004$$$::...There's still a bit of it I haven't explored, but even those gaps are insignificant, peaceful days.[lr]::
24615::$$$message_0181_0100_0005$$$::But anyway...::
24616::$$$message_0181_0101_0000$$$::"Liar? Who do you think I am? There's no way an Avenger would be an honest person."[lr]::
24617::$$$message_0181_0101_0001$$$::It's regrettable she called me a liar.[lr]::
24618::$$$message_0181_0101_0002$$$::Seriously, what does she think I am?::
924524::$$$message_9181_0077_0000$$$::"Hey there. Looks like you've pretty much remembered everything."[r]::

